   "source": [
    "## Loops\n",
    "A loop is used to execute a block of code repeatedly until a particular condition is met.\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine you want to print \"Hello\" 10 times. Instead of writing print(\"Hello\") ten times, you can use a loop.\n",
    "\n",
    "Python has two main types of loops:\n",
    "1. for loop\n",
    "2. while loop"
   ]
